The network in net/ re-implements Marigold V2 (https://github.com/huawei-bayerlab/marigold-v2, Apache License 2.0;
its NOTICE credits the Marigold files it derives from: Copyright 2023-2025 ETH Zurich, Apache License 2.0) without
diffusers, bitsandbytes and peft: the Qwen-Image-Edit-2509 transformer (Qwen team, Alibaba Cloud,
https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen-Image-Edit-2509, Apache License 2.0) with Marigold V2's depth LoRA folded in as
separate factors, and the Qwen-Image VAE with Marigold V2's fine-tuned decoder on a single frame.

The weights are not included. fastforks downloads one converted file (see card.toml): the transformer quantised to
NF4 (4 bit, blocks of 64, bitsandbytes' 16 code values, MIT) as Marigold V2 loads it, the LoRA factors, the
constants of the fixed timestep and of the fixed prompt (Qwen2.5-VL text embeddings shipped by Marigold V2, Apache
License 2.0), and the VAE as 2-D weights in bf16. Both originals and the converted file are Apache License 2.0.
